From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:18:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-husky: drop the
 soc_compatible descriptions

Stock's base DTBs label each /soc_compatible child with a description
string ("B0,FOPLP"). ABL matches on product_id, major, minor and
pkg_mode, and boots this tree without the labels, so drop them: the
node names already say the same, and dtbs_check no longer reports them.

Tested on a Pixel 8 Pro: the bootloader picks this tree and boots it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
index 449094128..105050a62 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
@@ -19,7 +19,6 @@ / {
 	 */
 	soc_compatible {
 		B0_FOPLP {
-			description = "B0,FOPLP";
 			product_id = <0x9865>;
 			major = <1>;
 			minor = <0>;
@@ -27,7 +26,6 @@ B0_FOPLP {
 		};
 
 		B1_FOPLP {
-			description = "B1,FOPLP";
 			product_id = <0x9865>;
 			major = <1>;
 			minor = <1>;
